Package: tolmix
Type: Package
Title: Tolerance Intervals for Random and Mixed Effects Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("J.", "Zhang", email = "zhangjc98@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes one-sided and two-sided beta-content and
    beta-expectation tolerance intervals for the distribution of a future
    observation under one-way random effects models and general linear
    mixed-effects models. Implements several approaches from the
    literature: the Mee and Owen (1983) <doi:10.1080/01621459.1983.10477008>
    one-sided limits, the Krishnamoorthy and Mathew (2004)
    <doi:10.1198/004017004000000031> generalized pivotal quantity method,
    the Hoffman and Kringle (2005) <doi:10.1198/106186005X78670> modified
    large sample two-sided intervals, and Satterthwaite-type and parametric
    bootstrap methods for models fitted with 'lme4' in the spirit of
    Francq, Lin and Hoyer (2019) <doi:10.1002/sim.8281>.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: stats
Suggests: lme4, reformulas
NeedsCompilation: no
